        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): stop retrying non-idempotent sends on post-connect-ambiguous errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nDiscord message creates can complete at Discord while the client receives a transport failure. Retrying the same non-idempotent create without a server deduplication key can deliver a duplicate message.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach direct Discord Create Message now receives a 24-character random nonce with `enforce_nonce: true`. The nonce is built once before the retry runner, so a retry returns the existing message rather than creating another. This covers text, media, components, stickers, polls, approvals, and voice messages.\n\nThe nonce-protected Create Message classifier keeps pre-connect failures, rate limits, and HTTP 502 retryable. Forum and media thread creation use the pre-connect-only classifier because Discord documents nonce enforcement only for Create Message, not the endpoint that creates a thread and starter message together.\n\n## Why this is the right boundary\n\nThe retry module still owns retry classification. Message construction owns the create nonce, which remains stable for all attempts of one logical create. Forum thread creation selects the narrower retry policy at its endpoint boundary. Idempotent REST operations retain the broad transient retry policy unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/discord/src/retry.test.ts extensions/discord/src/send.message-request.test.ts extensions/discord/src/send.creates-thread.test.ts extensions/discord/src/outbound-payload.contract.test.ts extensions/discord/src/client.test.ts extensions/discord/src/outbound-adapter.test.ts` passed with 134 assertions.\n- Scoped `tsgo`, `oxlint`, and `oxfmt --check` passed for the changed paths.\n- Structured closeout review completed with no actionable findings.\n\n## Real behavior proof\nBehavior addressed: HTTP 502 replay could duplicate direct sticker or poll creates, and could duplicate a forum/media thread creation.\nReal environment tested: the production Discord `RequestClient`, `createChannelMessage`, `createThread`, request serialization, retry runner, and a real localhost TCP HTTP connection on pristine main 1bcc4c5e70 and this patch; the controlled server records the first create before returning HTTP 502 and applies the Create Message nonce contract on retries.\nExact steps or command run after this patch: run `tsx --tsconfig tsconfig.json /tmp/discord-network-fault-proof.ts /root/openclaw-pr-discord-retry patched <sticker|poll|forum>`, with the identical command against `/root/openclaw` for pristine main.\nEvidence after fix:\n```\n# BEFORE (pristine main 1bcc4c5e70)\nmode=sticker | serverSideCreates=2 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-2 | requests=2\nmode=poll | serverSideCreates=2 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-2 | requests=2\nmode=forum | serverSideCreates=2 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-2 | requests=2\n\n# AFTER (this patch, identical HTTP 502 sequence)\nmode=sticker | serverSideCreates=1 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-1 | requests=2\nmode=poll | serverSideCreates=1 | send RESOLVED id=discord-msg-1 | requests=2\nmode=forum | serverSideCreates=1 | send REJECTED DiscordError | requests=1\n```\nObserved result after fix: sticker and poll retry the gateway-unavailable response to the nonce-matched original message, while forum creation surfaces the ambiguous result without replaying the endpoint.\nWhat was not tested: no request was sent to Discord production; the controlled network fault uses a local HTTP server and does not exercise Discord credentials, permissions, or rate limits.\n",
        "branch": "fix/discord-nonidempotent-send-retry",
